<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 23 November, from 1248 to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/seville" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seville.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1248">1248 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">778 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Seville surrenders to Ferdinand III of Castile</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege of more than a year, the Muslim city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-of-castile">Ferdinand III of Castile</a>. Its fall left the Nasrid kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> as the main surviving Muslim state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/crown-of-castile">Crown of Castile</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-of-castile">Ferdinand III of Castile</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1499">1499 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">527 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The pretender Perkin Warbeck is hanged at Tyburn</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Perkin Warbeck, who had claimed to be Richard, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>, the younger of the 'Princes in the Tower', was hanged after a failed escape. His death removed a persistent threat to Henry VII.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1644">1644 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">382 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Milton publishes Areopagitica</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John Milton issued Areopagitica, an unlicensed pamphlet arguing against Parliament's censorship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a>. It became a classic defence of freedom of the press.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1700">1700 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">326 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The papal conclave elects Giovanni Albani as Pope Clement XI</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A papal conclave elected Cardinal Giovanni Albani as Clement XI after a month's deadlock that ended with the death of the childless <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-spain">Charles II of Spain</a>. Expecting a political crisis, the cardinals chose a pope who would be seen as non-partisan.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-spain">Charles II of Spain</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1889">1889 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">137 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first coin-operated phonograph plays in San Francisco</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Louis <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gla">Glass</a> installed a coin-in-the-slot phonograph at the Palais Royale Saloon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a>. Listening through tubes, customers paid a nickel a song, the ancestor of the jukebox.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1914">1914 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The last US forces withdraw from Veracruz</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> forces left the Mexican port city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veracruz">Veracruz</a>, which they had occupied since April in response to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tampico">Tampico</a> Affair. The occupation contributed to the fall of General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victoriano-huerta">Victoriano Huerta</a>, who resigned in July.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-revolution">Mexican Revolution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Romania joins the Tripartite Pact</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripartite-pact">Tripartite Pact</a>, the alliance concluded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> on 27 September, and so formally joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis powers</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> had joined on 20 November; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a> followed on 24 November.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripartite-pact">Tripartite Pact</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis powers</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Doctor Who is first broadcast</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The BBC broadcast the first episode of Doctor Who, about a time-travelling alien in a police box. It became the longest-running science fiction television series in the world.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 23 November <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-x-of-castile"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfonso-x-of-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfonso X of Castile</span><span class="tp">1221–1284</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/anthonie-heinsius"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anthonie-heinsius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Anthonie Heinsius</span><span class="tp">1641–1720</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-clemente-orozco"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-clemente-orozco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Clemente Orozco</span><span class="tp">1883–1949</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/klement-gottwald"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/klement-gottwald.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Klement Gottwald</span><span class="tp">1896–1953</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-napoleon-duarte"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-napoleon-duarte.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Napoleón Duarte</span><span class="tp">1925–1990</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nicolas-maduro"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nicolas-maduro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nicolás Maduro</span><span class="tp">b. 1962</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 23 November <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-fei-of-jin"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Emperor Fei of Jin</span><span class="tp">342–386</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eadred"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eadred.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eadred</span><span class="tp">c. 923–955</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-duke-of-orleans"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-i-duke-of-orleans.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis I, Duke of Orléans</span><span class="tp">1372–1407</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/margaret-of-york"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/margaret-of-york.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Margaret of York</span><span class="tp">1446–1503</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/claude-lorrain"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/claude-lorrain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Claude Lorrain</span><span class="tp">c. 1600–1682</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/constantine-mavrocordatos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/constantine-mavrocordatos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Constantine Mavrocordatos</span><span class="tp">1711–1769</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-jourdan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jean-baptiste-jourdan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jean-Baptiste Jourdan</span><span class="tp">1762–1833</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-iii-of-the-netherlands"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-iii-of-the-netherlands.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William III of the Netherlands</span><span class="tp">1817–1890</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/aman-andom"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aman-andom.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Aman Andom</span><span class="tp">1924–1974</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
